  "id": "mental-chronometry",
  "term": "mental chronometry",
  "definition": "Mental chronometry is the study of the timing of cognitive processes, focusing on their temporal aspects. In this context, methods such as event-related potentials can be used to estimate when cognitive processes occur with high temporal precision.",
